  "goodToKnow": "Die Heimatstadt is your home town, where you grew up or feel you belong. Die Heimat is a famously hard-to-translate word: it means home and homeland, but with strong feelings of belonging, landscape and childhood. Since 2018, Germany's interior ministry has been officially called Bundesministerium des Innern und für Heimat. For a village, Germans say Heimatdorf. Plural: die Heimatstädte."
